gbg1(){return"This Policy may be updated at any time without prior notice. The current version will be made available within the Service. Continued use of the Service following any update constitutes acceptance of the updated Policy. It is the user's sole responsibility to review the current Policy."},
gbg2(){return"The following personal data is processed:\n\n\u2022 Email address \u2014 provided at account registration.\n\u2022 Portfolio data \u2014 stock holdings and transactions, manually entered by the user.\n\u2022 Journal entries \u2014 trading notes and reflections, manually entered by the user.\n\u2022 Goals \u2014 financial goals, manually entered by the user.\n\u2022 Weekly Ten \u2014 the filter saved by the user and the companies shown each week, kept so the same company is not shown again.\n\u2022 Authentication tokens \u2014 generated upon login, stored in device secure local storage.\n\u2022 Billing and subscription status \u2014 processed by the applicable app store platform (Apple App Store or Google Play). The developer does not receive or store full payment card details.\n\u2022 Crash diagnostic data \u2014 when an unhandled error occurs, the error message, stack trace, device type, OS version, and app version are transmitted to Sentry for debugging purposes. No portfolio data, financial figures, or user-identifiable information is included in these reports.\n\nNo advertising identifiers, location data, or device tracking data are collected. The developer does not engage in any form of user behaviour tracking."},
gbg3(){return"What Is Collected"},
gbg4(){return'This Privacy Policy applies to the Portfolio Keeper mobile application ("Service"). The Service is provided solely for personal entertainment and informal record-keeping and has no financial, investment, or advisory function whatsoever. The data controller is the individual developer of Portfolio Keeper, reachable via the Privacy Contact form in the app Settings. No data protection officer has been appointed. This policy is governed by Swedish law.'},
gbg5(){return"The Service does not use analytics, advertising networks, or third-party tracking SDKs of any kind. No tracking of users across apps or websites occurs. The crash reporting service (Sentry) described above is used solely for diagnosing application errors and does not track user behaviour or activity."},
gbg6(){return"No Tracking"},
gbg7(){return"Data is processed for the following purposes, each based on performance of the contract between the user and the developer (GDPR Art. 6(1)(b)):\n\n\u2022 Email address \u2014 to create and maintain the user account.\n\u2022 Portfolio data, journal entries, goals, and Weekly Ten filters and lists \u2014 to provide the core storage and display function of the Service.\n\u2022 Authentication tokens \u2014 to authenticate the user session.\n\u2022 Billing and subscription status \u2014 to verify access to premium features. This data is processed by the applicable app store platform; the developer receives only confirmation of subscription status.\n\nProvision of an email address is a contractual requirement for use of the Service. Users who do not provide it cannot use the Service."},
gbg8(){return"Purposes and Legal Bases"},
gbg9(){return"Data is retained for as long as the user maintains an account. Upon account deletion request submitted via the Privacy Contact form in app Settings, account data will be removed from active systems. Removal from backup systems may take additional time. The developer retains the right to retain data to the extent required by applicable law or for the establishment, exercise, or defence of legal claims."},
gbga(){return"Data Retention"},
gbgb(){return"If you are located in the European Economic Area, you have the following rights under GDPR with respect to your personal data:\n\n\u2022 Right of access (Art. 15)\n\u2022 Right to rectification (Art. 16)\n\u2022 Right to erasure (Art. 17)\n\u2022 Right to restriction of processing (Art. 18)\n\u2022 Right to data portability (Art. 20)\n\nTo exercise any of these rights, use the Privacy Contact form in app Settings (Settings \u2192 Privacy Contact). You also have the right to lodge a complaint with the Swedish Authority for Privacy Protection (Integritetsskyddsmyndigheten, imy.se)."},
